<title>FRANCE: Details of latest EU grain export/import balance.</title>
<headline>Details of latest EU grain export/import balance.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of EU grain export/import commitments as of October 8 in the July-to-June 1996/97 campaign, supplied by member country officials.</p>
<p>On October 10, the EU additionally granted exports of 192,450 tonnes of soft wheat, 185,786 tonnes of barley, 83,096 tonnes of rye and 98,500 tonnes of oats.</p>
<p>Figures ('000 tonnes) are based on officially communicated certificates and are subject to revision.</p>
<p>			 ---------1996/97-------  ------1995/96-----</p>
<p>			     1Jul96 to 8Oct96	1Jul95 to 8Oct95</p>
<p>			 EXPORTS  PCT(1) IMPORTS  EXPORTS    IMPORTS</p>
<p>  Soft wheat(grain)  1,465	51     187    2,889	  742</p>
<p>  Flour (2)	    1,351	84	 4    1,599	    8</p>
<p>Food aid</p>
<p>    - grain		224     124	 -	180	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   12	15	 -	 80	    -</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  2		   -	185	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	    9		   -	 43	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL SOFT WHEAT    3,063	62     191    4,976	  750</p>
<p>  Durum (grain)	   16		 112	  0	  454</p>
<p>  Semolina (3)	    59     257	 0	 23	    0</p>
<p>  Food aid		   1		   -	 41	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL DURUM WHEAT	76     119     112	 64	  454</p>
<p> ALL WHEAT	     3,139	62     303    5,040	1,204</p>
<p>  Barley (grain)     1,684     196	16	860	   65</p>
<p>  Malt (4)		 185   2,313	 0	  8	    0</p>
<p>  Donations		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL BARLEY	  1,869     215	16	868	   65</p>
<p>  Maize (grain)	   19   1,900     167	  1	  963</p>
<p>  Food aid		   0		   -	  0	    -</p>
